<http://data.silknow.org/object/2f11a53d-95c7-3e45-920c-10a1e25e076a/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Group of pieces of coloured silk needlepoint lace in the Bibila style, in mid-late 20th century museum frame, comprising: 1) Unfinished roundel of pink, green, white and claret,. 2) Partial border in vandyke form with pink and burgundy straight edge and vandykes in graduating dark-to-light tones of yellow, pink, green, red, and blue. 3) Group of 21 motifs mounted on piece of paper, mostly floral motifs, including rosebuds, a forget-me-not and a pansy, but also regular repeating pattern fragments."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/2f11a53d-95c7-3e45-920c-10a1e25e076a> .

